{#-
  Everything the image says as one line of text, ready for an `alt`
  attribute: newlines and runs of spaces become single spaces, since an
  attribute has no lines to break.

  Takes `var.max_chars`, the most characters to write, `0` for all of them. A
  longer text is cut at a word boundary and ends in an ellipsis, so that a
  reader hears a sentence rather than half a word.

  The text is written as it was read, not escaped, since where it is going is
  not this template's to know: a caller placing it in markup asks for
  `autoescape=html`.
-#}
{%- set flat = text | split | join(" ") -%}
{%- set limit = vars.max_chars | default(0) | number -%}
{%- if limit > 0 and (flat | length) > limit -%}
{#- The ellipsis is a character of the text too, so it is counted. -#}
{%- set kept = namespace(text="", full=false) -%}
{%- for word in flat | split -%}
{%- if not kept.full -%}
{%- set candidate = kept.text ~ (" " if kept.text else "") ~ word -%}
{%- if (candidate | length) <= limit - 1 -%}
{%- set kept.text = candidate -%}
{%- else -%}
{%- set kept.full = true -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{{ kept.text }}…
{%- else -%}
{{ flat }}
{%- endif -%}
